pulsar (0.1.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Initial Debian release.
  * Installs the pulsar Python module into the system dist-packages and the
    /usr/bin/pulsar launcher built from the [project.scripts] entry point.
  * Ships a .desktop entry with Exec already set to the installed binary
    rather than the PLACEHOLDER_EXEC_PATH the source template carries, so
    menu launchers work for anyone installing from the package.
  * Installs the icon set into the hicolor theme layout.
  * Depends on python3-tk (tkinter is imported at start-up), pulseaudio-utils
    (pactl) and pipewire (pw-dump, pw-top, pw-record).

 -- Skomesh <skomesh@users.noreply.github.com>  Fri, 16 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000

# RELEASE PROCEDURE / VERSION SINGLE SOURCE OF TRUTH
#
# The upstream version lives in exactly one place: the `version` key of
# [project] in pyproject.toml. debian/changelog carries a copy of it only
# because dpkg has nowhere else to read a package version from.
#
# To cut a release:
#
#   1. Update CHANGELOG.md and bump `version` in pyproject.toml.
#   2. Run `dch -v <new version>` and edit the generated entry. `dch` stamps
#      the RFC 2822 date and the maintainer address for you; keep the trailing
#      "-- Name <address>  Date" trailer line, dpkg-parsechangelog needs it.
#   3. Tag the git repository with the same version and build the orig tarball
#      so debian/source/format's "3.0 (quilt)" resolves:
#          git archive --format=tar.gz --prefix=pulsar-<version>/ \
#              -o ../pulsar_<version>.orig.tar.gz v<version>
#   4. Build:  dpkg-buildpackage -us -uc -b   (or use the full -S for a .dsc)
#
# Step 2 is the only error-prone one, so debian/rules contains a guard in
# override_dh_auto_build that compares `version` from pyproject.toml against
# the upstream version in this file and fails the build on a mismatch. A
# forgotten changelog bump stops the build; it does not produce a .deb whose
# filename says one version and whose METADATA says another.
#
# Note the first stanza uses revision -1: 0.1.0-1 is the first Debian
# packaging of upstream 0.1.0. Upstream version and Debian revision are
# distinct fields and must not be conflated -- the guard compares upstream
# versions only, stripping the Debian revision.